# Project Architecture Guidelines

## Clean Architecture Overview

### Architecture Principles
- **Separation of Concerns** - Each module has a single responsibility
- **Dependency Inversion** - Dependencies point inward toward business logic
- **Testability** - All components are easily testable in isolation
- **Scalability** - Modular structure supports team scaling
- **Maintainability** - Clear boundaries between features and logic

### Layer Structure
```
┌─────────────────────────────────────┐
│           Presentation Layer        │
│     (Feature Modules + UI Logic)    │
├─────────────────────────────────────┤
│            Domain Layer             │
│         (Business Logic)            │
├─────────────────────────────────────┤
│             Data Layer              │
│   (Network, Storage, Core Logic)    │
└─────────────────────────────────────┘
```

## Module Classification

### Feature Modules (Presentation Layer)
**Purpose**: User interface and user interaction logic
- `authentication-feature` - Login, biometric setup, wallet activation
- `dashboard-feature` - Home screen, quick actions, main navigation
- `issuance-feature` - Credential issuance flows and management
- `proximity-feature` - NFC and QR code sharing functionality
- `presentation-feature` - Credential presentation to verifiers
- `startup-feature` - App initialization and onboarding
- `common-feature` - Shared UI components across features

### Logic Modules (Domain & Data Layers)
**Purpose**: Business rules, data access, and core functionality
- `business-logic` - Core wallet business rules and use cases
- `core-logic` - Shared utilities, base classes, and common functionality
- `network-logic` - API communication and remote data sources
- `storage-logic` - Local data persistence and caching
- `authentication-logic` - Authentication and authorization logic
- `wallet-activation-logic` - Wallet setup and activation processes
- `assembly-logic` - Credential assembly and validation
- `analytics-logic` - Usage tracking and analytics
- `notification-logic` - Push notifications and messaging
- `ui-logic` - Shared UI components, themes, and design system
- `resources-logic` - Shared resources, strings, and assets
- `test-logic` - Testing utilities and shared test components

## Dependency Rules

### Module Dependencies
```kotlin
// ✅ ALLOWED DEPENDENCIES
authentication-feature → authentication-logic
authentication-feature → ui-logic
authentication-feature → resources-logic

dashboard-feature → business-logic
dashboard-feature → ui-logic
dashboard-feature → core-logic

business-logic → storage-logic
business-logic → network-logic
business-logic → core-logic

// ❌ FORBIDDEN DEPENDENCIES
core-logic → business-logic        // Core cannot depend on business
ui-logic → authentication-feature  // Logic cannot depend on features
storage-logic → network-logic      // Horizontal dependencies between data modules
```

### Dependency Direction
- **Features** depend on **Logic modules**
- **Logic modules** depend on **Core logic**
- **Core logic** has minimal external dependencies
- **No circular dependencies** between modules

## MVI Pattern Implementation

### ViewModel Structure
```kotlin
class AuthenticationViewModel @Inject constructor(
    private val authenticateUseCase: AuthenticateUseCase,
    private val biometricManager: BiometricAuthManager
) : BaseViewModel<Event, State, Effect>() {
    
    // State management
    override fun setInitialState(): State = State.initial()
    
    // Event handling
    override fun handleEvents(event: Event) {
        when (event) {
            is Event.LoginPressed -> handleLogin(event.credentials)
            is Event.BiometricPressed -> handleBiometricAuth()
        }
    }
    
    // Side effects
    private fun handleLogin(credentials: UserCredentials) {
        setState { copy(isLoading = true) }
        viewModelScope.launch {
            authenticateUseCase(credentials)
                .onSuccess { token ->
                    setState { copy(isLoading = false, isAuthenticated = true) }
                    setEffect { Effect.NavigateToDashboard }
                }
                .onFailure { error ->
                    setState { copy(isLoading = false, error = error.message) }
                    setEffect { Effect.ShowError(error.message) }
                }
        }
    }
}

// State definition
data class State(
    val isLoading: Boolean = false,
    val isAuthenticated: Boolean = false,
    val error: String? = null
) {
    companion object {
        fun initial() = State()
    }
}

// Events
sealed class Event {
    data class LoginPressed(val credentials: UserCredentials) : Event()
    object BiometricPressed : Event()
}

// Effects
sealed class Effect {
    object NavigateToDashboard : Effect()
    data class ShowError(val message: String) : Effect()
}
```

### Screen Composition
```kotlin
@Composable
fun AuthenticationScreen(
    viewModel: AuthenticationViewModel = hiltViewModel(),
    onNavigateToDashboard: () -> Unit
) {
    val state by viewModel.uiState.collectAsState()
    
    LaunchedEffect(Unit) {
        viewModel.effect.collect { effect ->
            when (effect) {
                is Effect.NavigateToDashboard -> onNavigateToDashboard()
                is Effect.ShowError -> {
                    // Show error snackbar or dialog
                }
            }
        }
    }
    
    AuthenticationContent(
        state = state,
        onEvent = viewModel::setEvent
    )
}

@Composable
private fun AuthenticationContent(
    state: State,
    onEvent: (Event) -> Unit
) {
    // UI implementation
}
```

## Repository Pattern

### Repository Interface
```kotlin
interface AuthenticationRepository {
    suspend fun authenticateUser(credentials: UserCredentials): Result<AuthToken>
    suspend fun refreshToken(token: RefreshToken): Result<AuthToken>
    suspend fun logout(): Result<Unit>
    fun observeAuthState(): Flow<AuthState>
}
```

### Repository Implementation
```kotlin
@Singleton
class AuthenticationRepositoryImpl @Inject constructor(
    private val networkDataSource: AuthNetworkDataSource,
    private val localDataSource: AuthLocalDataSource,
    private val securityManager: SecurityManager
) : AuthenticationRepository {
    
    override suspend fun authenticateUser(credentials: UserCredentials): Result<AuthToken> {
        return try {
            val encryptedCredentials = securityManager.encrypt(credentials)
            val response = networkDataSource.authenticate(encryptedCredentials)
            localDataSource.saveAuthToken(response.token)
            Result.success(response.token)
        } catch (e: Exception) {
            Result.failure(e)
        }
    }
    
    override fun observeAuthState(): Flow<AuthState> {
        return localDataSource.observeAuthToken()
            .map { token ->
                if (token != null && !token.isExpired()) {
                    AuthState.Authenticated(token)
                } else {
                    AuthState.Unauthenticated
                }
            }
    }
}
```

## Use Case Pattern

### Use Case Implementation
```kotlin
class AuthenticateUserUseCase @Inject constructor(
    private val authRepository: AuthenticationRepository,
    private val deviceController: DeviceController,
    private val analyticsRepository: AnalyticsRepository
) {
    suspend operator fun invoke(credentials: UserCredentials): Result<AuthToken> {
        // Validate device security
        if (!deviceController.isDeviceSecure()) {
            return Result.failure(SecurityException("Device not secure"))
        }
        
        return authRepository.authenticateUser(credentials)
            .onSuccess { token ->
                analyticsRepository.trackEvent(AnalyticsEvent.UserAuthenticated)
            }
            .onFailure { error ->
                analyticsRepository.trackEvent(AnalyticsEvent.AuthenticationFailed(error))
            }
    }
}
```

## Navigation Architecture

### Navigation Graph Structure
```kotlin
@Composable
fun AppNavigation(
    navController: NavHostController = rememberNavController()
) {
    NavHost(
        navController = navController,
        startDestination = "startup"
    ) {
        // Startup flow
        composable("startup") {
            StartupScreen(
                onNavigateToAuth = { navController.navigate("authentication") },
                onNavigateToDashboard = { navController.navigate("dashboard") }
            )
        }
        
        // Authentication flow
        composable("authentication") {
            AuthenticationScreen(
                onNavigateToDashboard = { 
                    navController.navigate("dashboard") {
                        popUpTo("authentication") { inclusive = true }
                    }
                }
            )
        }
        
        // Main dashboard with bottom navigation
        composable("dashboard") {
            DashboardScreen(
                onNavigateToIssuance = { navController.navigate("issuance") },
                onNavigateToPresentation = { navController.navigate("presentation") }
            )
        }
        
        // Feature-specific navigation graphs
        issuanceNavGraph(navController)
        presentationNavGraph(navController)
        proximityNavGraph(navController)
    }
}
```

